{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And by way of the plain sense</b>, Scripture warns concerning the man with a nocturnal emission that he must go outside the entire camp, for the reason stated: that HaShem walks among us to save us, and the camp is holy, and that our hearts should be directed toward the Holy One, blessed be He, and we await His salvation, and not rely on the arm of flesh. And the same is the reason for covering excrement, for the entire camp is like the sanctuary of YHWH. And from this we learn regarding a place of prayer, that we must distance ourselves from excrement by four cubits, and from anything visible to the eyes. But our Sages interpret homiletically (Pesachim 68a): 'And he shall go outside the camp; he shall not come inside the camp' — this refers to the camp of Leviyyah and the camp of the Shekhinah, when the Ark would be with them there. And likewise the covering of excrement, according to their opinion (Berakhot 22b; 25a), is in a place where one mentions the Name to pray or to recite the Shema. If so, then this too is a warning that He doubled concerning the camp, that it not all be unrestricted like the camps of the nations. And these commandments are also clearly explained. And the reason for covering excrement is that excrement is not like a tumah that defiles its place and penetrates and rises upward; rather, it is forbidden to see it at the time of prayer and when the heart is cleaving to the honored Name, because repulsive things produce disgrace in the soul and corrupt the intention of the pure heart, and when it is hidden from the eye of the beholder, there is no harm."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "I resolved להקב\"ה as 'the Holy One, blessed be He,' the standard expansion of this reverent abbreviation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:54:28.289931493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}